# Publish library on push

When the user asks to push to GitHub (or create a PR that will be pushed):

1. Run `npm run publish:library` from the repo root first. That copies the Mac `library/` songs and `library/gigs.json` setlist into `client-library/`.
2. Stage the resulting `library/gigs.json` and `client-library/` changes with the rest of the push. Practice only sees this published copy.
3. Do not leave setlist or song-library edits uncommitted on a push. The desk and the band page must ship the same show.

Do not skip this because the files look like leftovers.
